			"Message": "refactor(Output): Reorganize all source files into semantic directory structure\n\nRelocate the entire content of the Output element's `Source` directory from flat CamelCase filenames to a nested, PascalCase hierarchical structure. This massive reorganization affects ESBuild configurations, Copy/Transform plugins, Polyfills, and Asset stylesheets.\n\nEvery file is moved to reflect its functional domain (e.g., `Source/Plugin/Transform/Replace/Electron/IPC/Service.ts`, `Source/Polyfill/IPC/Renderer/Shim.ts`, `Source/Asset/Style/Editor/GPU/Layer.css`). All file contents remain unchanged (100% similarity), preserving the logic of the build pipeline and polyfilling strategies established in recent commits.\n\nThis change aligns the physical file system with the logical modularity of the codebase, ensuring all file names and directory paths strictly adhere to the project's PascalCase naming convention. It enhances navigability and sets the stage for the next phase of build configuration updates.",
			"SHA": "b44e67e8d068446db2ec132e1bfead172a69555d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T17:26:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				416,
				9
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Stabilize webview rendering and port capture on WKWebView\n\nIntroduce `PatchWebviewIframeServiceWorker` to the build pipeline and enhance `CELExposeAccessor` to prevent extension webview hangs and `setHtml` deadlocks under Tauri/WKWebView.\n\n1. **ServiceWorker Patch:** Force `disableServiceWorker = true` and relax strict `parentOrigin` hash/crypto checks in the webview bootstrap (`pre/index.html`). WKWebView rejects ServiceWorker registration on `vscode-webview://` protocols, causing the bootstrap script to await a rejected promise and bail. The plugin injects markers to bypass these checks, ensuring the iframe shell renders immediately.\n2. **Port Capture Hook:** Implement a global `window.addEventListener` interceptor in `CELExposeAccessor` to mirror the `webview-ready` message port association into a `globalThis.__CEL_WEBVIEW_PORT_MAP__`. This safeguards against occasional port-transfer drops in the native layer, allowing the workbench to recover communication channels even if the standard handler misses the event.\n3. **Pipeline Alignment:** Update `Apply/Pipeline.ts` and `prepublishOnly.sh` to reflect the new semantic directory structure for service files, ensuring build targets match the refactored source layout.\n\nThese changes resolve persistent stalls where extension views and sidebars remain stuck at the `pre/index.html` chrome.",
			"SHA": "8f141784d9e9dd5bd6370117bb1af283d09ea634"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T17:26:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				414,
				10
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Reorganize service files into semantic directory structure\n\nRestructure the flattened service directory in the Output element to reflect the logical grouping of CodeEditorLand (CEL) components and external dependencies.\n\nMove previously flat service files (`CELExposeAccessor`, `CELExtensionsScannerService`, `DevLog`, etc.) into their respective namespace folders under `Source/Service/` (e.g., `CEL/Expose/`, `CEL/Null/`, `Tauri/Main/Process/`). The `ApplyPipeline.ts` file is also moved to `Source/Apply/`. All file contents remain unchanged (100% similarity), preserving the PascalCase naming conventions and logical behavior established in recent formatting commits.\n\nThis reorganization improves navigability and aligns the file system with the architectural modularity of the CEL service layer, facilitating future development and maintenance of the bundled artifacts.",
			"SHA": "85e32b1a6abe85a4a29799e4b3b97008daa343a9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T15:09:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				397,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Fix webview iframe hanging by patching ServiceWorker and event activation\n\nAddress critical UI stalls where extension webviews and sidebar panes remain stuck at the bare chrome (`pre/index.html`).\n\n1. **Webview Shell Patch (Plugin):** Add `PatchWebviewIframeServiceWorker` to the ESBuild pipeline. Under Tauri 2 + WKWebView, the custom `vscode-webview://` protocol rejects ServiceWorker registration, causing the bootstrap script to await a rejected promise and bail with `fatal-error`. This plugin forces `disableServiceWorker = true` and soft-fails strict `parentOrigin` hash checks that fail on custom protocols, ensuring the iframe renders correctly.\n\n2. **Extension Activation Patch (Service):** Enhance `CELExposeAccessor` to short-circuit `IExtensionService.activateByEvent` for `onView:*` events. Since Land's `*` activation pass loads all extensions at boot, waiting for specific view events (which block `WebviewViewPane.activate`) creates a deadlock in Cocoon. Immediate resolution prevents sidebar stalls.\n\nThese changes resolve hangs in extension webviews and sidebar views without forking the upstream workbench bootstrap logic.",
			"SHA": "57b2a1a56c41c5e61dcc2dd421aaf5a555a80d37"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T11:29:14Z",
